class Solution {
public:
    int searchInsert(vector<int>& nums, int target) {
        int left = 0;
        int right = nums.size() - 1;

        while (left <= right) {
            int mid = left + (right - left) / 2;

            if (nums[mid] == target)
                return mid;
            else if (nums[mid] < target)
                left = mid + 1;
            else
                right = mid - 1;
        }

        return left;
    }
};

Intuition: Since the array is sorted, binary search can quickly find the target or its correct position.
Algorithm: Compare the middle element and eliminate half of the search space each time.
Key Idea: When the loop ends, left is the insertion position.
Time Complexity: O(log n)
Space Complexity: O(1).
